#: ../../source/developers/apps/index.rst:7
msgid ""
"These pages explain how SEPAL decides which app code to run and how that "
"code reaches the platform — useful when you want to add an app, ship a "
"new version of an existing one, or package a reusable environment for a "
"notebook or workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/apps/index.rst:14
msgid ""
"The set of apps SEPAL runs is curated in the `dfguerrerom/sepal-apps-"
"catalog <https://github.com/dfguerrerom/sepal-apps-catalog>`__ "
"repository. Getting an app onto SEPAL — or updating one — means opening a"
" pull request there. For docker apps, the catalog also pins the *exact "
"commit* SEPAL will run; for jupyter apps, the catalog records the "
"``branch`` and SEPAL still runs the tip of that branch. The pages below "
"walk through both flows."
msgstr ""

